--- 
title: "stdlib.base64 Tutorial"
author: IVANLI2412
date: 2026-11-23
abstract: Base64 encoding/decoding per RFC 4648 with URL-safe variants and validation.

# stdlib.base64 Tutorial

Base64 encoding/decoding per RFC 4648.

## Functions
- `encode(data: bytes) -> str`: Standard Base64 with padding
- `decode(text: str) -> bytes`: Standard decode
- `encode_url(data: bytes) -> str`: URL-safe (RFC 4648 §5), no padding
- `decode_url(text: str) -> bytes`: URL-safe decode
- `encode_no_pad(data: bytes) -> str`: Standard without padding
- `decode_no_pad(text: str) -> bytes`: Decode without requiring padding
- `is_valid(text: str) -> bool`: Validate standard Base64
- `is_valid_url(text: str) -> bool`: Validate URL-safe Base64
- `encoded_length(input_len) -> int`, `decoded_length(encoded_len) -> int`
- `max_encoded_length(input_len) -> int`, `max_decoded_length(encoded_len) -> int`

## RFC 4648 Test Vectors
"" -> ""
"f" -> "Zg==" (std), "Zg" (url)
"fo" -> "Zm8=" (std), "Zm8" (url)
"foo" -> "Zm9v" (std), "Zm9v" (url)
"foob" -> "Zm9vYg==" (std), "Zm9vYg" (url)
"foobar" -> "Zm9vYmFy" (both)
